# Pseudocode of Python Projects

Simple and concise pseudocode for all projects in this repository.

## 1. Molarity Calculator
```text
START
DISPLAY "Molarity Calculator"
REPEAT
  INPUT moles or "exit"
  IF input is "exit" → STOP
  INPUT volume in mL
  IF volume <= 0 → DISPLAY error and CONTINUE
  CONVERT mL to liters
  CALCULATE molarity = moles / liters
  DISPLAY molarity rounded to 4 decimals
UNTIL stopped
END
```

## 2. Phone Number Details
```text
START
IMPORT phone number library
DEFINE GET_PHONE(number)
  PARSE the number
  IF number is invalid → RETURN error
  FIND number type, location, carrier, and time zones
  RETURN the details
END FUNCTION
CALL GET_PHONE with the given number
DISPLAY the details
END
```

## 3. Projectile Motion Calculator
```text
START
SET gravity = 9.81 m/s²
REPEAT
  INPUT initial velocity or "exit"
  IF input is "exit" → STOP
  INPUT launch angle
  CONVERT angle to radians
  CALCULATE horizontal and vertical velocity
  CALCULATE flight time, maximum height, and range
  DISPLAY the results
  OPTIONALLY calculate height at a given time
UNTIL stopped
END
```

## 4. Projectile Ball Simulation
```text
START
IMPORT Pygame and create the game window
SET gravity, ball position, velocity, and launch position
WHILE game is running
  CHECK keyboard/mouse events
  IF mouse is pressed → START dragging
  IF mouse is released → CALCULATE launch velocity and START flight
  IF ball is flying → APPLY gravity and UPDATE position
  IF ball hits ground or leaves screen → RESET ball
  DRAW ground, ball, and launch line
  UPDATE screen at 60 FPS
END WHILE
QUIT Pygame
END
```

## 5. Time-Angle Sun-Earth Calculation
```text
START
SET total degrees = 360 and total hours = 24
CALCULATE hours per degree
CONVERT hours per degree to minutes
CALCULATE time for 5 degrees
DISPLAY all calculated values
END
```

## 6. Turtle Rainbow Flower
```text
START
IMPORT Turtle and Colorsys
SET drawing speed and black background
SET hue = 0
REPEAT 16 times
  REPEAT 18 times
    CONVERT HSV color to RGB and set turtle color
    INCREASE hue
    DRAW two circular arcs to form a petal
    TURN turtle 180°
  END REPEAT
  DRAW an arc to move to the next section
END REPEAT
KEEP the window open
END
```

## General Flow
```text
START → INPUT/SET VALUES → PROCESS/CALCULATE → DISPLAY/DRAW → REPEAT IF NEEDED → END
```